WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:05.350
Man vs. Wild star Bear Grylls has actually
got quite a few side projects that help keep

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:08.160
that cash flowing even when he's not in front
of the camera.

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:12.080
Here are some of the highlights from his financial
journey over the years that have helped him

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:13.900
mint his fortune in spades.

00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:19.180
While it isn't everything, the successful
survivor's television career has obviously

00:00:19.180 --> 00:00:22.460
served as a critical piece in founding his
financial fortune.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:28.280
Man vs. Wild, his first blockbuster show,
was watched by over a billion viewers.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:32.500
But in more recent years, the Discovery Channel
sensation managed to leverage his growing

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:37.739
popularity into several other shows, including
Running Wild, in which he's taken numerous

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:40.380
celebrities with him on his adventures in
the wilderness.

00:00:40.710 --> 00:00:43.260
"Let's, uh, let's really discuss our plan
here…

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:45.980
“I think on these journeys it's always step
by step...Really.”

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:46.480
“Right.

00:00:46.760 --> 00:00:48.820
You don't think we should stop and discuss
a plan."

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:54.700
According to The Richest, it's estimated that
Grylls raked in a whopping $30,000 per episode

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:58.020
and that was just during his stint on Man
vs. Wild.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.560
Since then, the numbers only seem to have
gone up.

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:05.540
Needless to say, there's no doubt that Mr.
Grylls' personal fortune has received a healthy

00:01:05.540 --> 00:01:08.190
boost from the years he's spent in front of
the camera.

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:12.800
"I think if somebody said to me at age 7 that
I could have a job that involved climbing

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:14.580
trees and getting muddy, I would've thought,
'heaven.'"

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:20.940
Television career aside, Grylls has also made
several savvy real estate investments over

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:25.080
time, the most impressive of which has to
be the island he owns in Wales.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:30.119
But we're not talking about a dirt-rich celebrity
dropping a ton of cash on a fancy new island

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:31.020
just for fun.

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:36.320
According to The Telegraph, Grylls actually
bought the island in 1999, over five years

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:38.480
before Man vs. Wild started up.

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:43.420
The island, which he considers one of his
best investments, covered 20 acres that came

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:45.220
with a cottage in need of renovation.

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:49.700
He spent the four years following the purchase
scrimping and saving up enough money to make

00:01:49.700 --> 00:01:50.340
repairs.

00:01:50.700 --> 00:01:55.850
In 2008, Bear estimated he'd spent 100,000
pounds on the project and that it was worth

00:01:55.850 --> 00:01:57.140
a cool million.

00:01:58.389 --> 00:02:01.829
Call it old school if you'd like, but when
The Telegraph asked how he preferred to pay

00:02:01.829 --> 00:02:04.500
for things, Gryll's answer was short and simple:

00:02:04.960 --> 00:02:08.020
"Debit card because then there's no risk of
getting into debt."

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:13.120
Even when he was still getting started, Bear
refused to fall victim to the "swipe and forget

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:16.060
it" mentality that plagues the modern consumer-driven
world.

00:02:16.550 --> 00:02:20.740
While he may have the gusto to buy a fixer-upper
island, that doesn't mean the man spends money

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.020
at the drop of a hat.

00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:26.360
In fact, he's demonstrated an ability to be
cautious enough to ensure that his personal

00:02:26.380 --> 00:02:28.060
fortune remains in the black.

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:34.840
Mr. Grylls has carefully curated his persona
as a tough-as-nails survivalist, but he's

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:38.480
also built up an impressive side career as
an accomplished author.

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:44.220
His lengthy list of book topics includes survival
tips, lifestyle advice, his own personal experiences,

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:47.000
and even a number of children's series.

00:02:47.489 --> 00:02:52.760
A catalog of books that big by one man is
an incredible sight to behold on its own nevermind

00:02:52.760 --> 00:02:54.980
the fact that for Grylls, it's a side hustle.

00:02:55.220 --> 00:03:00.019
Sure, he might already own an island and be
paid tens of thousands of dollars per episode,

00:03:00.019 --> 00:03:04.260
but when you consider the fact that he'd reportedly
sold over three million copies of his books

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:09.569
by 2015, the amount of influence that "Bear
Grylls the author" has played in building

00:03:09.569 --> 00:03:13.220
his fortune becomes a bigger deal than just
some cash on the side.

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:18.840
For a man who's spent much of his life showing
off his skills by surviving with next to nothing,

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:22.140
the guy seems to have managed to make bank
on his merch sales.

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:26.300
According to the Evening Standard, he was
estimated to have brought in over three million

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:29.040
pounds in merchandising in 2015 alone.

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:33.560
So what exactly does a man who eats maggots
and pees on his clothes sell?

00:03:34.060 --> 00:03:38.720
As it turns out, the Bear Grylls merch line
includes everything from his famous Bear Grylls

00:03:38.740 --> 00:03:43.240
Ultimate Pro Knife to a water bottle that
also serves as a lamp and power source.

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:47.500
While merch sales are hard to pin down on
a consistent basis, there's no doubt that

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:51.220
the sale of his own products has created some
lucrative side income for Grylls.

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:56.440
While there's no doubt that Grylls has a boatload
of money, he's made it clear from early on

00:03:56.450 --> 00:04:00.430
that just because he has more than he needs
doesn't mean he throws money away with the

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:01.660
little transactions.

00:04:02.090 --> 00:04:06.660
As he told The Telegraph, he's tried not to
convert the money he earns from his U.S. shows

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:10.180
into British pounds because he doesn't want
to lose cash in the transition.

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:14.880
Instead, Grylls put his U.S. dollars into
an international investment fund, where it

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:19.100
can gain value without the need to go through
any switch over to U.K. currency.

00:04:19.240 --> 00:04:23.960
While it seems like a small detail, it comes
from a mind that is clearly focused on making

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:26.440
the best possible decisions at every turn.

